  "notes": "{涼|すず}む means to cool oneself or enjoy cool air, especially during hot summer days.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし})\n- Pattern: Xで{涼|すず}む (cool off at X)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {縁側|えんがわ}で{涼|すず}む (to cool off on the veranda)\n- {木陰|こかげ}で{涼|すず}む (to cool off in the tree shade)\n- {夕涼|ゆうすず}み (enjoying the evening cool) [noun]\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nEnjoying the cool breeze ({涼|すず}む) is a traditional Japanese way of coping with hot summers. Activities include sitting on the {縁側|えんがわ} (veranda), listening to {風鈴|ふうりん} (wind chimes), or going out for {夕涼|ゆうすず}み in the evening.\n\nRELATED:\n- {涼|すず}しい (cool, refreshing) [i-adjective]",
